  "_comment": "Bytes are 0x-hex, lower case; inside a file's text (envelope, item, header) bytes are base64 (RFC 4648 §4, padded). Generated by clients/clientkeys/scripts/profile-vectors.mjs (src/profile.js); never edit by hand. Random inputs are fixed: rnd(name, n) = the first n bytes of keccak256(\"scaas/profile/vectors/<name>/0\") ‖ keccak256(\"scaas/profile/vectors/<name>/1\") ‖ …; the labels are in the generator. Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-27-user-profiles.md (§4, §6, §7.1, §7.2, §10.1) and the plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-27-user-profiles.md (\"Pinned formats\"). UNAUDITED. envelope.json: kdf_bounds (the general bounds, the test set m 8192 t 1 p 4 only under feature test-hooks, else ProfileFormat); pass rows (OpaqueString bytes as ua-rs passphrase_bytes, Argon2id v0x13 32 bytes, KEK_pass = HKDF-SHA256(salt empty, info \"scaas.profile.wrap.v1\"), the public JSON, the wrap AD = \"scaas/ua/v1/keywrap\" ‖ 0x01 ‖ lp(\"scaas.profile.wrap\") ‖ public JSON, pass = nonce ‖ AES-256-GCM-SIV(KEK_pass, nonce, DEK_p, AD), 60 bytes); one row at the default set 64 MiB / 3 / 4, the others at the test set; the platform wrap (K_plat from the platform secret, domain scaas.profile.platform); sub_keys K_label, K_item, K_name; labels (AD lp(scaas.profile.label) ‖ be16(1) ‖ lp(id)); whole envelope files (one protected at the default set; one with migration pending); wrap_refusals (Aead, each beside its control); name_hint (opens). kdf_sets: the default and the test set.",
